{
 "item": "W46.fix-capture-tags",
 "method": "Tags drafted from each page image by Claude Opus 5.5 (four subagents, 24 pages each) against the schema in \"attributes\" (levels 0 absent, 1 present, 2 severe); audited with the draft in view by Claude Sonnet 5.5, which changed 11 of 1344 cells; tagged again blind by Claude Sonnet 5.5, which disagreed with the audited draft on whether a defect is present in 173 cells on 81 pages; each of those cells settled by a third look (Claude Opus 5.5, the image and both notes in view). Where the two agreed on presence the audited draft's level stands. Not owner-labelled (STATE Phase 2 decision 2). All subscription calls; no money.",
 "attributes": [
  "neighbour",
  "edge_cut",
  "hand",
  "perspective",
  "curl",
  "shadow",
  "glare",
  "low_light",
  "motion_blur",
  "defocus",
  "colour",
  "show_through",
  "faint_ink",
  "mixed"
 ],
 "definitions": "|---|---|\n| neighbour | anything in the frame that is not the target page: a neighbouring or underlying page's text, folder or box label, archive call-number slip, ruler, colour card, another document. 2 = it carries readable text a reader could transcribe as if it were the page |\n| edge_cut | part of the target page (its text or its edge) is outside the frame |\n| hand | fingers or a hand in frame |\n| perspective | page edges visibly non-rectangular or rotated by more than about 5 degrees (keystone, skew) |\n| curl | page bent, curled, folded or bound-book curvature, so text lines visibly curve |\n| shadow | a shadow (phone, hand, fold) falls across the text area |\n| glare | a specular highlight or washed-out patch |\n| low_light | the whole image is dim, under-exposed or noisy |\n| motion_blur | directional smear of strokes |\n| defocus | soft, out-of-focus strokes (all directions) |\n| colour | a colour cast, or coloured / dark stock (yellow, pink, blue, purple paper; white type on colour) |\n| show_through | text or marks from the overleaf or the page beneath visible through the paper |\n| faint_ink | faint, faded, carbon-copy, pencil or very light type |\n| mixed | more than one content kind on the page: typed plus handwritten annotations, stamps, form plus handwriting, clipping pasted on a typed page, chart with hand labels |",
